f 1035 #uuid "4a33a1d4-8dfa-5e25-8ed4-4aa1496ac8a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1031 "Complementary Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1033 1639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050661 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5d18c23d-b718-5823-8edb-6d9b84a6faab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050754 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186213248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050754 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186213249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050754 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186213250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050754 #edb/ref 1031 "Non-Adjacent Complementary Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050754 #edb/ref 1033 6207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050754 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "63e063dc-074b-516d-ac51-9e38d630b9e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114978 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2620" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114978 #edb/ref 1071 "The angles $\\angle a$ and $\\angle b$ are complementary angles. If $m \\angle a = 37^\\circ$, what is the measure of $\\angle b$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af3cc0f3-0971-5b26-b9bc-eda04373f225" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114978 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/18/18d67b5d6d05c29fdf286406cdb8f1615f623c942c55d414b0655c8ac0ef242b.png)\n\nSince $\\angle a$ and $\\angle b$ are complementary, the sum of their measures is equal to $90^\\circ$. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠a + m∠b &= 90^{∘} \\\\\n37^{∘} + m∠b &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠b &= 90^{∘} - 37^{∘} \\\\\nm∠b &= 53^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114979 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2623" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114979 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $x$, given that $\\angle{A}$ and $\\angle{B}$ are complementary, and that\n$m\\angle{A} = 3x, \\qquad m\\angle{B} = 4x-8^\\circ\\,$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114979 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5532a2f6-e93e-5c85-bea6-be5961424ba3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114979 #edb/ref 1074 "Since angles $\\angle{A}$ and $\\angle{B}$ are complementary, we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle A + m \\angle B = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A + m∠B &= 90^{∘} \\\\\n3x + (4x - 8^{∘}) &= 90^{∘} \\\\\n7x - 8^{∘} &= 90^{∘} \\\\\n7x &= 98^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 14^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114980 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2627" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114980 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\angle A$ and $\\angle B$ be two complementary angles. If $m \\angle B = 2m \\angle A$, find $m \\angle B$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114980 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83b57ed2-9933-51be-8e12-bfd95ea36be0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114980 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $\\angle A$ and $\\angle B$ are complementary angles, we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle A + m \\angle B = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nm \\angle B = 2m \\angle A\n$$\n\nwe obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A + m∠B &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠A + 2m∠A &= 90^{∘} \\\\\n3m∠A &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠A &= 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠B &= 2m∠A \\\\\n&= 2(30^{∘}) \\\\\n&= 60^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114981 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2629" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114981 #edb/ref 1071 "In the figure below, $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles. If $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$ and $m \\angle COB = 50^\\circ$, find $m \\angle AOD$.\n\n![](images/60/60c48e8ce5fd289f6aa7b80cfd5a99db1adf9a0603e6162c1fb5b4dcf1a7e15d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c3ef1dc-0262-5bed-9980-1672ca0e6f62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114981 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠AOC + m∠COB &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠AOC + 50^{∘} &= 90^{∘} \\\\\nm∠AOC &= 40^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$, we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle BOD = m \\angle AOC=40^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠AOD &= m∠AOC + m∠COB + m∠BOD \\\\\n&= 40^{∘} + 50^{∘} + 40^{∘} \\\\\n&= 130^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding an Unknown Complementary Angle Given the Other Angle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186114978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115402 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "72e4154b-bb7a-5029-b698-98588634d677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115403 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115403 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115403 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding an Unknown Quantity Using Complementary Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115403 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186114979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115403 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b6f00614-8fb3-5aed-8730-2118f31ab4d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115404 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115404 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115404 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115404 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding an Unknow